outram-park-fork-offbeat
Part of Outram Park (outram-park-backend).

This crate is an independent fork / Rust translation of OFFBEAT — the OpenFOAM
Fuel BEhaviour Analysis Tool
  https://gitlab.com/foam-for-nuclear/offbeat
  https://foam-for-nuclear.gitlab.io/offbeat/
OFFBEAT is a multi-dimensional, finite-volume nuclear fuel-performance solver
built on OpenFOAM, developed under the `foam-for-nuclear` project by the
Laboratory for Reactor Physics and Systems Behaviour (LRS) at EPFL, the
Laboratory for Reactor Physics and Thermal-Hydraulics (LRT) at the Paul
Scherrer Institute, and the MEDAL group at Texas A&M University.

Primary reference:
  "The OFFBEAT multi-dimensional fuel behavior solver", Nuclear Engineering and
  Design. Publisher record:
  https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0029549319304479
  (No DOI is recorded here because it was not independently verified; cite the
  DOI from the publisher record rather than from this file.)

