Every Rust source file in this crate that derives from OFFBEAT carries a
provenance header naming the upstream source file(s), the upstream project,
the upstream commit, the copyright holder, and the license, per the workspace
attribution rule. As of 2026-07-30 all 44 source files carry such a header.

The upstream tree is NOT vendored into this repository. Porting is done by
reading a read-only clone kept outside this working tree; no OpenFOAM or
OFFBEAT C++ source is copied into the repository.

SCIANTIX — not ported here. Upstream OFFBEAT vendors SCIANTIX, a separate
0-D grain-scale fission-gas code from Politecnico di Milano distributed under
the MIT license (https://github.com/sciantix/sciantix-official). No SCIANTIX
source is copied, vendored or translated into this crate. What the `fgr` module
ports is OFFBEAT's own coupling shim (`fgrSCIANTIX`, `fgrSCIANTIXRIA`), which
is GPL-3.0 OFFBEAT code. If SCIANTIX itself is ever ported into this crate, the
ported files MUST carry the MIT copyright notice and permission text, and this
NOTICE must be updated to record the dual license lineage — MIT-licensed code
may be combined into a GPL-3.0 work, but its notice may not be dropped.

STATUS — SCAFFOLD / EARLY, NO HUMAN V&V. The mechanics layer is verified
against closed-form linear-elasticity solutions and the crate's 361 unit tests
pass, but nothing in it has been validated against OFFBEAT output, against the
upstream `Cases/Verification` suite, or against fuel-irradiation data, and no
human has reviewed it. Per RESPONSIBLE_USE.md, AI-assisted output is untrusted
draft material until a human reviews it. Nothing here may be described as
validated fuel performance.

